id:                     E442
trigger_tool:           libtool|clang|ld.lld|readelf
phase:                  linking
error_signature:        -no-undefined.*plugin|undefined reference.*host|cannot find.*host.*library|plugin.*dlopen.*undefined

severity:               2
category:               linking, packaging, plugins, runtime-contract
match_keywords:         host-loaded plugin, private host ABI, unresolved host symbols, libtool module, no-undefined, dlopen, ELF DYN, plugin entry points
title:                  Preserve the host ABI contract when packaging a host-loaded plugin independently

root_cause:             An upstream plugin target is normally linked inside the full host application build, so its build rules require the in-tree host library and reject unresolved symbols. A standalone package that builds only the plugin has no such host library, while the real runtime contract expects the host process to resolve those symbols when loading the module.
affected_scope:         Host-loaded ELF plugins extracted from a larger application tree when the host application ABI is not a separately published package and the plugin exposes identifiable loader entry points.
verification_cmd:       Use readelf to require an ELF DYN module and the expected exported plugin entry points, then validate loading inside the real host separately when that application is available.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           model-host-as-runtime-contract
rec_description:        Build only the plugin target, remove the fully-resolved-link policy only for that module, omit unavailable in-tree host linkage, and document the exact host ABI/version expected at load time.
rec_command:            readelf -h plugin.so && readelf --dyn-syms -W plugin.so
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-and-targeted-source-adjustment

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      publish-host-sdk-package
fallback_description:   If the host project provides a stable public plugin SDK or import library, package that SDK separately and link against it while retaining a runtime dependency on the matching host version.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          separate-dependency-package

forbid_1_pattern:       stub.*host|fake.*host|dummy.*host
forbid_1_reason:        A stub can make the link succeed while masking the loader contract and producing a module that fails or behaves incorrectly in the real host.
forbid_1_consequence:   Package validation passes against an artificial ABI that the production host does not provide.
forbid_2_pattern:       allow.*undefined.*all|disable.*no-undefined.*global
forbid_2_reason:        Unresolved symbols are valid only for the identified host-loaded module, not for every library produced by the project.
forbid_2_consequence:   Genuine dependency and link defects in unrelated targets are hidden.

principles:             P010, P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               doc/E337.md
last_updated:           2026-08-24
source_event:           abiword-plugin-gdict 3.0.8 OHOS plugin-only build and Shadow r20 validation
